/__pycache__/
/apks/
/bin/
/mop_out/
/out/
/lib_tmp/
/tmp/
/apks_mini/
/results/

# data/: the corpora and everything the campaigns wrote over them — 279 GB, of
# which data/results/ alone is 275 GB. None of it is versioned, and none of it
# was ignored either, so `git status` carried ~500 untracked entries and a
# careless `git add .` would have tried to commit the lot.
#
# The heavy paths are named one by one rather than ignoring /data/ wholesale,
# because the directory is NOT all artifacts: the ~45 *_filters/ directories are
# small APK selection lists, 29 of them already tracked, and data/apks/ mixes
# 113 versioned .txt lists in with 169 .apk binaries and their .json siblings.
# Ignoring the parent would keep the tracked files working (gitignore does not
# untrack) but would silently swallow the next list someone adds beside them.
/data/results/
/data/validacao_full/
/data/validacao_ajc/
/data/validacao_ajc_v2/
/data/compat_dataset/
/data/apks/*.apk
/data/apks/*.apk.json

# experimento-gov: heavy run artifacts (raw logcats/tasks.json, instrumented
# APKs, snapshots). Root /results/ and /out/ rules are anchored to rv-android
# root and do NOT cover these nested paths, so ignore them explicitly.
/experimento-gov/results/
/experimento-gov/results.zip
/experimento-gov/results_g2/
/experimento-gov/instrumentation/

# experimento-e3-decisiva: the decisive run writes 120 result trees here (raw
# logcats, tasks.json, coverage). Same reason as experimento-gov above — the
# root /results/ rule does not reach nested campaign directories.
/experimento-e3-decisiva/results/

# experimento-rearch-aperv: the gh97 A/B gate campaign, 7.6 GB of result trees
# plus the per-container logs it streamed while running. Same reason as the two
# campaigns above, and it was left out of this list until 2026-08-07 — which
# left those gigabytes one pathspec-less `git add` away from the index on a
# branch several sessions commit to. The consolidated artefacts of the same
# campaign (verification_report.md, per_apk_paired.csv, tel_proxies.csv) are
# deliberately NOT ignored: they are the gate's evidence and are versioned.
/experimento-rearch-aperv/results/
/experimento-rearch-aperv/results_smoke/
/experimento-rearch-aperv/container_logs/

# experimento-comp162: 1458 runs (162 APKs x 3 arms x 3 reps), which at the ~5 MB
# per run the cmp163 measured lands around 7.5 GB of result trees. Listed here
# BEFORE the campaign runs, not after — the rearch entry above went in two days
# late and spent that window one pathspec-less `git add` from the index. What the
# campaign produces under consolidado/ is deliberately NOT ignored: those CSVs are
# the evidence, and they are kilobytes.
/experimento-comp162/results/
/experimento-comp162/results_smoke/

# experimento-gh104: the same 1458-run grid as comp162, re-run against the new
# specification set, plus a stage-1 weaving tree the earlier campaigns kept
# outside the repo. Three heavy paths, all listed BEFORE the campaign runs:
# the campaign result trees (~7.5 GB), the smoke ones, and instrumentacao/results/,
# which holds eight per-shard scratch dirs (woven_*.dex, monitor-build/, lib_tmp/)
# plus the woven APKs themselves. What lands under consolidado/, monitores/ and
# filters/ is deliberately NOT ignored: the gate JSONs, the msg_diff CSV, the
# monitor digests and the shard lists are the evidence, and they are kilobytes.
/experimento-gh104/results/
/experimento-gh104/results_smoke/
/experimento-gh104/instrumentacao/results/

# gh52: instr-cli fat jar is auto-copied by the Maven build (design D9);
# not versioned because it's a build output of
# rvsec/rvsec-android/rvsec-instrumentation-dexlib2/cli.
modules/rv-instrumentation-dexlib2/lib/*.jar

# AspectJ compiler crash dumps — produced by ajc when weaving fails on
# specific classes. Useful for debugging individual instrumentation runs
# but transient; not part of the source tree.
ajcore.*.txt

# Calibration datasets (instrumented APKs + SA JSONs, ~658MB)
modules/rv-agent-validation/data/calibration_dataset/
modules/rv-agent-validation/data/calibration_dataset_v2/


